  "payload": {
   "provider": "Dr. Deborah Malone",
   "specialty": "family medicine",
   "page_count": 2,
   "pages": [
    {
     "page": 1,
     "text": "**CERTIFIED TRANSLATION - original in Tagalog**\n\n**Translator: L. Chen, #36705**\n\n---\n\n**Patient:** Jacob Foster\n\n**DOB:** 07/12/1945\n\n**Sex:** M\n\n---\n\n**Attending Physician:** Dr. Deborah Malone\n\n**Specialty:** Family Medicine\n\n**Practice:** Johnson Group Medical Group\n\n---\n\n**Medical Record Summary**\n\n---\n\n**Medical Record 1**\n\n**Date:** 26/09/2025\n\n**Reason for Visit:** Upper Respiratory Infection (URI)\n\n**Blood Pressure:** 122/68 mmHg\n\n**Weight:** 114 lbs\n\n**Chief Complaint:** The patient, Jacob Foster, presented with symptoms of an upper respiratory infection, including nasal congestion, sore throat, and cough. He reported that these symptoms began three days ago and have been progressively worsening. The patient also mentioned occasional mild shortness of breath but denied any chest pain, fever, recent travel.\n\n**Physical Examination:** On examination, Jacob Foster appeared well. His vital signs were stable. The physical examination of the chest was clear, with no wheezing or crackles noted. His throat showed mild erythema without exudate. Nasal passages were congested with clear rhinorrhea. Lungs were clear to auscultation bilaterally. The remainder of the physical examination was unremarkable.\n\n**Diagnosis:** Upper Respiratory Infection\n\n**Plan:** \n- Provided symptomatic treatment including hydration and over-the-counter decongestants.\n- Advised rest and advised to follow up if symptoms worsen.\n\n---\n\n**Medical Record 2**\n\n**Date:** 11/02/2025\n\n**Reason for Visit:** Back Strain\n\n**Blood Pressure:** 107/66 mmHg\n\n**Weight:** 100 lbs\n\n**Chief Complaint:** Jacob Foster reported a back strain that occurred approximately two weeks ago during a gardening activity. He described the pain as localized in the lower back, with occasional radiating discomfort into the right buttock. The was exacerbated by movement and relieved with rest.\n\n**Physical Examination:** On examination, Jacob Foster's lumbar spine showed mild tenderness to palpation, particularly over the paraspinal muscles. There was no evidence of bruising or swelling. Range of motion in the lumbar spine was mildly restricted. The neurological examination was intact, with no signs of radiculopathy.\n\n**Diagnosis:** Back Strain\n\n**Plan:**\n- Recommended nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drugs (NSAIDs) for pain relief.\n- Advised rest and gradual return to activities.\n- Prescribed physical therapy referral for strengthening exercises.\n\n---\n\n**Medical Record 3**\n\n**Date:** 28/06/2024\n\n**Reason for Visit:** Gastroesophageal Reflux Disease (GERD)\n\n**Blood Pressure:** 117/70 mmHg\n\n**Weight:** 101"
    },
    {
     "page": 2,
     "text": "lbs\n\n**Chief Complaint:** Jacob Foster reported symptoms of GERD, including heartburn and regurgitation, which began approximately three weeks ago. The symptoms occur predominantly after meals and at night, often leading to disturbed sleep.\n\n**Physical Examination:** On Jacob Foster appeared well. Abdominal examination was unremarkable with no tenderness or organomegaly. The remainder of the physical examination was within normal limits.\n\n**Diagnosis:** GERD\n\n**Plan:**\n- Prescribed famotidine 20 mg twice daily.\n- Recommended lifestyle modifications including dietary changes (avoiding spicy and fatty foods) and elevating the head of the bed during sleep.\n- Advised to follow\n"
    }
   ],
